ELETE attempt, the directory removed under a persistent 429, a skip, or a collection error.", "complexity": 2, "created_at": "2026-11-15T16:13:43.541737+00:00", "updated_at": "2026-11-20T17:46:55Z", "foreman_note": "\n\nPM REPAIR 2026-11-16 (auger-pm tick auger-pm-2026-11-16-20-51-14): acceptance rewritten so every arm names a real path, a runnable command and a recognizable outcome; current-state probes measured on main@37a9206c before the edit. Gated with acceptance_gate.py validate (PRE-ADD GATE) before writing.\n\nWorker report claimed grep count 8 for 429; measured count in tests/smoke.sh is 6 before and after - the file was not modified, so the discrepancy is in the worker's grep scope, not in the deliverable. Foreman re-verified the count directly.", "capability_tags": ["teardown", "smoke", "regression"], "depends_on": [], "worker_status": "pending", "commit_hash": "a2cdd76", "guard_result": "PASS", "ci_result": "SKIP", "worktree": null, "branch": null, "worker_summary": "Landed as a2cdd76 on main (worktree /home/kara/worktrees/auger-AUG-171, branch wt/AUG-171, base 4da3a39). Two hermetic tests in tests/test_smoke_teardown.py drive the REAL helper: _heredoc_body() extracts the ns_helper python heredoc out of tests/smoke.sh and executes it, so the 429 re-entry at smoke.sh:157-158 ('if not ok and \"HTTP 429\" in why: ok, why = drop(ns)') is the code under test. Red-proved both ways: with the re-entry condition disabled both tests fail, restored they pass. 'python3 -m pytest -q tests/test_smoke_teardown.py' -> 13 passed; '-k 429' -> 2 passed; ruff check + ruff format --check clean; smoke.sh grep count for 429 unchanged at 6 (test-only change). gitreins tier-2 verdict fd... run 2057a615 = PASS.", "evidence_run_id": "2057a615"}
 {"status": "complete", "id": "AUG-172", "title": "[P1] serve/API external spec consumption is unavailable live", "detail": {"fingerprint": "a2c6ca819aea568490e26fd4b83aaa7a1f4d0ecc6541444e06b93cb75ca832f6", "evidence": [{"run_id":"004065e3","ts":"2026-11-26T13:03:40Z"}]}, "priority": "P1", "source": null, "reasoning": "AUG-166 live external-agent probe: serve health responds, but the documented embedding search route returns an empty HTTP reply after the substrate query starts; the read-first API has no route for the XML spec corpus or spec blocks, and POST /check did not return within 20s. This blocks build-time consumption of spec context through serve/api.", "review_notes": null, "ts": null, "acceptance_criteria": "PASS: an external curl-only agent resolves the active specs corpus, fetches one block and receives a bounded verdict.\nPROBE (recipe in docs/qa/aug172-fix-proof.md, run from /tmp): start DUCKBRAIN_URL=http://localhost:3000 /home/kara/auger/venv/bin/python3 /home/kara/auger/auger.py api --host 127.0.0.1 --port 38755 ; then curl -s -o /dev/null -w '%{http_code} %{time_total}' http://127.0.0.1:38755/health expect 200 in under 1.0s; curl -s http://127.0.0.1:38755/api/ns/auger/specs expect 200 with a count field at or above 1; curl -s http://127.0.0.1:38755/api/ns/auger/specs/SPEC-GRAPH-CORPUS expect 200 with the block body; curl -s -m 20 -X POST -H 'Content-Type: application/json' -d '{\"question\":\"what does SPEC-GRAPH-CORPUS require about graph edges?\",\"limit\":3}' http://127.0.0.1:38755/api/ns/auger/check expect HTTP 200 carrying a bounded verdict (an explicit UNKNOWN fail-closed verdict is a PASS; a 20s timeout is a FAIL).\nFAILIF: 404, 502, an empty body, or /api/ns/auger/check exceeding its 10s budget without a bounded verdict. ROUTE CORRECTION: the check endpoint auger.py registers is POST /api/ns/auger/check (namespace segment then 'check'); a bare POST /check is not a route and answers 404 'no such route: /check' by design, so the earlier wording made this arm unpassable and invited a duplicate-alias 'fix'.", "complexity": 1, "created_at": "2026-11-15T21:49:00.88944+00:00", "updated_at": "2026-11-26T13:03:40Z", "foreman_note": "specs route implemented + /check bounded: retrieval 3s cap, JEV 10s cap with explicit fail-closed UNKNOWN verdict. Independent parent re-proof: /health 0.02s, /specs 200 0.06s, /check 200 3.93s (was 20s timeout). docs/qa/aug172-fix-proof.md. Tier1-only disclosed.\n\nFALSE-CLOSEOUT WITHDRAWN 2026-11-16 (goal driver, measured). This row was flipped to complete citing run bad8aaea, a tier1-only verdict graded on the SHARED checkout with working_tree_dirty_path_count=677: tier1 tests exit_code 2 -> FAIL, tier2 SKIPPED, pass_class=tier1-only, passed=false, and its lifecycle task id carries a suffix (AUG-*-SUFFIX) rather than this row id. That is the AUG-175 hazard, not evidence. Status restored and the non-admissible run id withdrawn from detail.evidence; a clean-tree judged PASS against this row id is required before any closeout.\n\nPM REPAIR 2026-11-16 (auger-pm tick auger-pm-2026-11-16-20-51-14): acceptance rewritten so every arm names a real path, a runnable command and a recognizable outcome; current-state probes measured on main@37a9206c before the edit. Gated with acceptance_gate.py validate (PRE-ADD GATE) before writing.\n\nPM VERIFIED 2026-11-16: fix proof present for all four arms (docs/qa/aug172-fix-proof.md: health 200 0.004201s, specs 200 0.187123s count 12, block 200 0.000684s SPEC-GRAPH-CORPUS, check 200 3.020544s verdict UNKNOWN jev_used=false). Close requires a clean-tree judged PASS against THIS row id (the withdrawn run bad8aaea was tier1-only on a 677-path dirty tree).\n\nPM PASS8 2026-11-20 (tick auger-pm-2026-11-20-09-16-17) DISPATCHABILITY REPAIR: AC4 named `POST /check`, a route the server never registers, so the arm could only ever measure 404 and a worker following it would have filed a phantom bug or added a duplicate alias route. Re-pointed at the registere